# "{U}, Sacrifice this creature: The next spell you cast this turn can't be countered." Bot1 casts Theorist's Proxy on turn 3
# (its enters trigger empowers a Jace token), then pays {U} and sacrifices it (the sacrifice is a cost, so the Proxy is in the
# graveyard while the ability is on the stack). Bot1 then casts two Lightning Bolts at Bot2, who answers each with Counterspell. The first
# Bolt is marked as it is cast (CR 601.2, 611.2c): the Counterspell resolves and does nothing (CR 701.5a) and the Bolt deals 3. The
# effect is used up by that spell, so the second Bolt is countered. The Proxy being gone does not undo the effect, and the Jace token
# it made stays.

